1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,545
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:08,466
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,593
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,637
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:18,893
[Atoy] Ah, sorry,
I just got distracted by your bag.

7
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:20,478
But it looks like it's missing a stud…

8
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:22,897
like this?

9
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:23,898
What puzzles me more,

10
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:25,525
is if it's true,

11
00:00:25,608 --> 00:00:27,110
then what was her motive?

12
00:00:27,193 --> 00:00:30,572
Was Martina in the office the other day?

13
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:31,740
[Ria] <i>Yes.</i>

14
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:33,408
<i>I have a picture…</i>

15
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:34,492
<i>You can see her in the background.</i>

16
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:37,912
I saw it under the console table
when I cleaned.

17
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:41,458
[attorney] <i>There are many bags</i>
<i>with studs like this.</i>

18
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,877
Looks like Attorney is right, 'Son.

19
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,755
Are you sure she believed
I was in the office?

20
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:47,839
Of course, ma'am.

21
00:00:47,922 --> 00:00:50,675
I even showed her the selfie,
while you were busy at work.

22
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:53,636
I was there. I couldn't do anything, bro!

23
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,889
And now, I'm just looking
for someone to blame!

24
00:00:55,972 --> 00:00:58,808
[Paldo] Stop blaming yourself.
What's wrong with you?

25
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:00,727
[Audrey, in English] <i>I want to apologize.</i>

26
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:03,480
[in English] For accusing me
of killing Tonet,

27
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:07,275
or for being so hateful
towards me and your brother?

28
00:01:07,358 --> 00:01:08,902
But just because we're family

29
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:11,154
doesn't mean I'll side with what's wrong.

30
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:13,907
Mommy, let's just go on vacation.

31
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:16,034
And my birthday is coming soon.

32
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:18,161
Let's celebrate there instead?

33
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:19,829
[in English] Okay, my dear. Yes.

34
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:21,790
[in English] Um, wherever you want to go.

35
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:25,210
Come on, let's go to the room, baby, okay?

36
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:26,461
Don't cry anymore.

37
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:28,755
PREVIOUSLY

38
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:31,382
[music swells]

39
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:33,843
[music fades]

40
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:39,891
[crickets chirping in the distance]

41
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:46,022
[Ibyang] Sister Tonet.

42
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:48,191
Sister Tonet.

43
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:51,653
Please show yourself to me.

44
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,739
Yoo-hoo!

45
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:58,785
You haven't gone up to heaven yet, right?

46
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,870
You were just buried.

47
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:05,542
Maybe you want a midnight snack.

48
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:08,169
Puff pastry, your favorite.

49
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:11,840
[frantic music playing]

50
00:02:14,425 --> 00:02:15,760
Sister Tonet?

51
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:18,555
Is that you?

52
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:21,808
[music swells]

53
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:24,310
[shrieks]

54
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:26,062
[Atoy] Son of a thread.

55
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:28,982
Ibyang, what are you doing here?
It's midnight.

56
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:30,483
Why aren't you asleep?

57
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:33,361
And what's with the candles?

58
00:02:33,444 --> 00:02:35,446
What are you doing now?

59
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:40,410
I want Sister Tonet
to let me feel her presence.

60
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:42,036
[melancholic music playing]

61
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:44,455
Miss Cita said

62
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:48,376
she showed herself
to Brother Emerson in the hospital,

63
00:02:48,459 --> 00:02:50,128
so…

64
00:02:50,211 --> 00:02:51,838
I'm calling her.

65
00:02:52,797 --> 00:02:55,425
I brought her favorite puff pastry.

66
00:02:58,553 --> 00:02:59,470
Ibyang.

67
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:07,395
You can't just call a person's soul
like you're calling a dog,

68
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:08,771
okay?

69
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:11,941
I just wanted to try.

70
00:03:13,818 --> 00:03:16,654
I miss Sister Tonet.

71
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:21,284
Why did she leave us so soon?

72
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:27,582
I wish I knew the answer to that.

73
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:34,964
But one thing I'm sure of, Ibyang,

74
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:37,342
no matter what happens,

75
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,053
I will never abandon you,

76
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:43,014
and I will never leave you.

77
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:45,266
[sentimental music playing]

78
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:46,184
Okay?

79
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:49,604
All right.

80
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:52,315
Go to sleep now. Go up to your room.

81
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,078
Go.

82
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:07,080
[Ibyang] Okay.

83
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:09,749
[Atoy, in English] Good night.

84
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,168
[music fades]

85
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:16,089
[phone vibrating]

86
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:18,591
Hello?

87
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:20,301
Who's this?

88
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:23,972
Janine.

89
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:26,557
Oh, why?

90
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:28,726
What's the problem?

91
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:31,980
[suave theme music playing]

92
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:58,131
[music concludes]

93
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:03,303
- [Gemma] Welcome to Amor Fati Lake resort,
- Oh wow!

94
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:05,138
- [Audrey] Thank you.
- Ms. Audrey and Ms. Janine!

95
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,472
[in English] I love it.

96
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:08,474
[in English] Oh, matching!

97
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:10,685
[in English] Oh, here you go, dear.

98
00:05:10,768 --> 00:05:12,520
- [in English] Cheers!
- Mommy.

99
00:05:13,146 --> 00:05:14,147
[in English] Thank you.

100
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:16,733
[in English] Anything for you, my dear.

101
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:19,485
Um, Mommy,

102
00:05:19,569 --> 00:05:21,279
I also have a surprise for you.

103
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:22,238
Mmm?

104
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:26,451
- To make this vacation perfect.
- Mmm.

105
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:28,745
[light music playing]

106
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:29,787
[Janine] Ta-da!

107
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:32,290
I invited Daddy.

108
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:33,708
Atoy?

109
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:38,337
Mommy, I called Daddy,

110
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:41,340
so, my birthday
will be our family bonding,

111
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,342
and we'll all be complete.

112
00:05:45,303 --> 00:05:46,387
[titters]

113
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:48,973
I have another surprise for you.

114
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:55,813
[Audrey] Ibyang.

115
00:05:56,856 --> 00:05:59,108
[unsettling music]

116
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,026
Ibyang?

117
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:03,362
Daddy, why is she here?

118
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:05,656
Janine, she has no one at home.

119
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,742
No one to watch over her.

120
00:06:07,825 --> 00:06:10,411
And also, it's so that
she can relax a bit too.

121
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:13,414
She's been so sad since Tonet passed away.

122
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,167
I don't like you.

123
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:17,710
Send her home, Daddy!

124
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:19,337
She's not part of the family!

125
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:20,338
Janine, shh.

126
00:06:20,421 --> 00:06:23,257
Janine, don't say that.

127
00:06:24,258 --> 00:06:26,010
Janine, you will be siblings.

128
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,428
I will adopt her.

129
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:29,514
She will take my surname too.

130
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:31,015
So, you will be siblings.

131
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,350
No!

132
00:06:32,433 --> 00:06:35,061
I'm your only child, Daddy!

133
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,065
- I'll talk to her.
- I'll handle it.

134
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,526
Janine, come here.

135
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:43,820
[pensive music playing]

136
00:06:43,903 --> 00:06:44,737
[Atoy] Come here.

137
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:46,531
Come here.

138
00:06:47,865 --> 00:06:50,535
Janine, I don't like what you're doing.

139
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:53,538
If you were raised like that before…

140
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:58,126
it won't work with me now. Okay?

141
00:06:58,209 --> 00:07:00,586
Because I don't want you to grow up a brat

142
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:01,796
and disrespectful to others.

143
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:07,635
I want you to apologize to Ibyang
and to your mommy.

144
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:11,806
[tense music playing]

145
00:07:12,932 --> 00:07:14,225
Janine.

146
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:26,529
[birds chirping]

147
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:27,905
[Atoy] Janine?

148
00:07:28,698 --> 00:07:29,657
Janine!

149
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:32,785
[phone recording, in English] <i>I'm sorry,</i>
<i>all circuits are busy now.</i>

150
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:34,787
What's this? I can't reach her!

151
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:36,456
There's no signal here.

152
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:39,333
What did you say to the child?

153
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,752
I just scolded her a little.

154
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,881
You know kids like that.
They need to be taught lessons early,

155
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:46,966
so they don't grow up spoiled.

156
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:49,051
You know,

157
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:50,678
it's a good thing you're here.

158
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:54,140
I can't discipline her the way you do.

159
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:59,145
I see how kind Ibyang is
because of your guidance.

160
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:02,523
[in English] You know, I think you'll be
a really good father to her.

161
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:03,900
[light music playing]

162
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:06,235
That one? [chuckles softly]

163
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,820
She's mischievous too.

164
00:08:08,905 --> 00:08:12,408
I hope you find her a mother.

165
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:15,661
So you'll have a partner in raising her.

166
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:20,166
It's not necessary. I can handle it.

167
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:22,752
Atoy, Ibyang is a girl.

168
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:24,879
She needs a mother figure.

169
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:27,715
[in English] You know, someone who will be
a good role model for her.

170
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:29,425
You should get married.

171
00:08:30,092 --> 00:08:31,302
[music fades]

172
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:32,512
She idolizes you.

173
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:35,264
[light music playing]

174
00:08:35,348 --> 00:08:37,225
Um… No, no. I don't mean
you should marry me, okay?

175
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:40,061
What I mean is, she mentioned to me once

176
00:08:40,144 --> 00:08:41,562
that she looks up to you.

177
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:43,105
Like she idolizes you,

178
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:44,232
something like that.

179
00:08:45,942 --> 00:08:47,109
Janine?

180
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:54,408
Where could she be?

181
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:57,036
[in English] Ah, um, sir, excuse me.

182
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,414
Did you notice a little girl?

183
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:02,500
Uh, long hair, eight years old.

184
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:05,545
- Wearing a pink dr--
- If your child is unruly,

185
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:07,547
don't bring her here just to lose her.

186
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:09,549
[in English] Sorry.

187
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,634
I didn't mean for my child to go missing.

188
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:14,554
You bear a child
and you can't even watch her.

189
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:17,557
[in English] Good morning, sir!

190
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:20,977
Gemma! Gemma!

191
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:22,603
- [Gemma, in English] Yes, ma'am?
- Who was that?

192
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:25,731
Ah. That was Sir Leon.

193
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,441
Um, that's just how he is.

194
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:29,986
Mmm, grumpy and weird.

195
00:09:30,653 --> 00:09:34,574
Actually, he's been renting near
your cabin for a month now.

196
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:38,244
He just doesn't like
being disturbed or hear any noise.

197
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:40,329
Then why rent here?

198
00:09:40,413 --> 00:09:42,415
He knows there are many guests.

199
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:44,792
He should've vacationed in a cave instead.

200
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:46,335
Yes, ma'am.

201
00:09:46,419 --> 00:09:48,588
Uh, I'll go ahead.
I'll look for Janine too.

202
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:50,673
- Okay. Thank you.
- Hmm-mm.

203
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,259
Where is that girl?

204
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:54,385
Janine.

205
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,099
[Gemma] Janine?

206
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:01,309
Hey!

207
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,060
So, you're just here!

208
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,980
Your mommy and daddy are looking for you.

209
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,857
Let them.

210
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,151
Let them look for me.

211
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:11,235
[unsettling music playing]

212
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:12,778
Daddy annoys me.

213
00:10:13,362 --> 00:10:15,740
He even brought that annoying Ibyang.

214
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:17,992
You're just staying here?

215
00:10:18,075 --> 00:10:19,410
All right.

216
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:21,912
They might go boating without you.

217
00:10:22,455 --> 00:10:25,333
I'll just tell them you're here sulking.

218
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,500
No.

219
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:29,962
I should be included.
This is my birthday vacation!

220
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:32,882
[sighs] Then go to your parents.

221
00:10:32,965 --> 00:10:34,967
Apologize to your daddy.

222
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:40,264
Behave, so you won't
get scolded anymore. Hmm?

223
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,892
[suspicious music playing]

224
00:10:47,521 --> 00:10:48,981
[music fades]

225
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:52,151
[Ibyang] Hey, Janine!

226
00:10:54,945 --> 00:10:57,365
Ibyang, let's talk.

227
00:10:58,491 --> 00:11:02,370
It's my birthday.
So, can I be with my parents?

228
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:05,998
[in English] Uh, okay?

229
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:08,334
Mmm, you're with them anyway.

230
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:09,669
[pensive music playing]

231
00:11:09,752 --> 00:11:12,713
Yes, of course.
But I don't want you to come with us!

232
00:11:13,547 --> 00:11:16,634
But Daddy can't send you home.

233
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:19,887
So, can you, Ibyang…
Just know your place, please.

234
00:11:20,471 --> 00:11:22,890
Give me a moment with my family

235
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,475
because we're the OG family.

236
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:27,520
This is the only time
I'll be with them, so…

237
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:32,066
make it your birthday gift to me,
Ibyang, please. Can you?

238
00:11:32,149 --> 00:11:34,819
[pensive music playing]

239
00:11:35,569 --> 00:11:36,862
All right.

240
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:37,947
[in English] Deal.

241
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:40,199
[in English] Happy birthday.

242
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,451
Birthday your face!

243
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:47,206
[Janine] Ouch.

244
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:49,458
Son of a-- Hey!

245
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,127
[ominous music playing]

246
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:52,420
So stupid.

247
00:11:53,045 --> 00:11:54,088
Why are you angry?

248
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,798
You're the one who bumped into me.

249
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:59,468
Hey, you.

250
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:01,178
I'll fight with kids, okay?

251
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:02,638
Don't test me!

252
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:04,181
Sorry.

253
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:06,016
Please don't be mad at her.

254
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,269
I'll apologize for her.

255
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:11,313
Hey, don't meddle!

256
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,899
Fine, leave now!

257
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,276
Go!

258
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:20,990
[music fades]

259
00:12:21,073 --> 00:12:25,536
[tense music playing]

260
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:34,170
[footsteps tapping]

261
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:38,090
[snoring]

262
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:42,261
[Karla] Really now.

263
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:50,394
Karla!

264
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:52,938
What's happening?

265
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:56,525
Don't sleep on the sofa.

266
00:12:57,109 --> 00:12:58,903
Buy me some beer first.

267
00:12:59,653 --> 00:13:00,654
Come on.

268
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:02,490
[Karla] Don't you want coffee first?

269
00:13:03,073 --> 00:13:04,867
Take a bath, brush your teeth,

270
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:06,994
look for a job!

271
00:13:07,077 --> 00:13:08,370
Ah, that's easy!

272
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:09,955
I'll do all that!

273
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:12,666
Just buy me some liquor

274
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:15,503
so my headache will go away.

275
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:16,504
Go on. Buy it.

276
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:19,381
[pensive music playing]

277
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:22,051
Oh? What are you waiting for?

278
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:25,095
My head hurts. To make it go away! Buy it.

279
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:27,848
[music swells]

280
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:34,480
[music fades]

281
00:13:34,563 --> 00:13:36,148
Oh, Janine!

282
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:37,483
- Oh, thank you.
- [Janine] Mommy.

283
00:13:37,566 --> 00:13:39,860
Mommy, wh-- where's Daddy?

284
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,695
[Audrey] He's still looking for you!

285
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:45,199
[clicks tongue] Janine, child…

286
00:13:45,282 --> 00:13:48,160
Don't get used to always walking out

287
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:51,080
whenever you don't like
what's being said to you.

288
00:13:51,163 --> 00:13:55,084
Your daddy just wants you
to be raised properly.

289
00:13:56,043 --> 00:13:57,378
[in English] I'm sorry.

290
00:13:58,379 --> 00:14:00,422
Is Daddy still mad at me?

291
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,551
He's not mad at you, dear.

292
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:07,596
Um, Mommy, Ibyang and I are okay now.

293
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,098
We've reconciled.

294
00:14:09,181 --> 00:14:11,809
I also apologized to her.

295
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:12,977
[Audrey mutters]

296
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:14,562
Oh, wow.

297
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:16,438
[sneaky music playing]

298
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:18,023
Um, right, Ibyang?

299
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:20,860
Uh, we're okay now.

300
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:25,114
We don't want any trouble
during my birthday vacation.

301
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:27,908
- Right?
- Uh, yes.

302
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:28,909
We're okay now.

303
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:32,413
[in English] That's very good.
I'm so happy to hear that.

304
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:35,791
Let's just forget
what happened earlier, okay?

305
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:40,838
[in English] We can officially start
your birthday vacation right now!

306
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:42,965
I'll call your daddy.

307
00:14:43,048 --> 00:14:45,801
I'll tell him we'll meet
at the boating area, okay?

308
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,678
Yay! Let's go boating!

309
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:50,222
[bright music playing]

310
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:54,101
[line ringing]

311
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:57,021
Please.

312
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:59,648
Don't sell liquor or beer
to my father anymore.

313
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:01,400
Not even rubbing alcohol.

314
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:03,694
He's been drunk for days now.

315
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:06,572
Since he lost his job,
he's just been drinking.

316
00:15:06,655 --> 00:15:09,992
Uh, don't worry. I'll tell my old buddies.

317
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:11,994
Because I've stopped drinking liquor

318
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:15,873
since I was forbidden
by San Antonio de Padua.

319
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:18,709
All right, child. I know the stores here.

320
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:21,337
I'm already disgusted with him.

321
00:15:22,379 --> 00:15:24,840
He smells so bad. He doesn't bathe.

322
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:28,802
Um, Karla, if you're
disgusted with the smell,

323
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:31,722
I have a suggestion, okay? Don't get mad.

324
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:33,682
Invite your father to drink.

325
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:35,809
Then, you guys will go against
each other in a shot-drinking contest.

326
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:36,727
[chuckles]

327
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:39,521
Ah, Nestor, you're not helping.

328
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:42,858
Karla, why do you seem unhappy?

329
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:44,944
Your father is here.

330
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:47,780
You know, when you were little,

331
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:50,950
when he didn't come home,
you missed him right away.

332
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:54,870
Now that he's here,
it's like you want to throw salt at him.

333
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:56,455
That was before.

334
00:15:57,122 --> 00:15:58,666
I got used to not being noticed.

335
00:15:58,749 --> 00:16:00,626
Often even being hit.

336
00:16:01,543 --> 00:16:03,253
I'd rather he wasn't here.

337
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:07,591
I never felt like I had a father.

338
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:11,595
Sir Delfin, I considered him my father.

339
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:15,599
He and Brother Atoy
are the decent men in my life.

340
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:18,894
[gentle music playing]

341
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:21,730
All right. I'll go now.

342
00:16:22,439 --> 00:16:24,692
[music fades]

343
00:16:25,526 --> 00:16:27,236
You and your suggestions. Oh, come on.

344
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:28,988
My suggestion was fine, right?

345
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:32,074
- It was a suggestion.
- But not like that.

346
00:16:32,157 --> 00:16:36,370
[bright music playing]

347
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:40,708
- If we go straight here, is it safe?
- [Ibyang] Tatoy!

348
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:42,209
I'll row, okay?

349
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:43,502
[dramatic sting]

350
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:46,505
Did you forget
your birthday gift to me, Ibyang, huh?

351
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:48,257
[dramatic sting]

352
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:51,343
What's that?

353
00:16:51,427 --> 00:16:54,972
Um, she said she won't join the boating.

354
00:16:57,516 --> 00:16:58,475
Oh?

355
00:16:58,559 --> 00:16:59,476
Yes.

356
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:03,188
I just suddenly got hungry.

357
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:08,819
Ah, I saw the clubhouse sandwich earlier.

358
00:17:09,486 --> 00:17:11,655
It looked delicious.

359
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:13,490
Really?

360
00:17:13,574 --> 00:17:16,243
- Yes, she's sure.
- [Atoy] All right.

361
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:17,494
Ah, Ma-- Marie…

362
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:19,038
Take care of this child
for the meantime, okay.

363
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:20,664
- Just feed her.
- Okay.

364
00:17:20,748 --> 00:17:22,499
[Atoy] Maybe three, whatever.

365
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:23,584
Come on, Janine.

366
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:26,211
- Let's go?
- [Atoy mutters]

367
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:28,172
[pensive music playing]

368
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:29,965
[Audrey] Ahh!

369
00:17:30,674 --> 00:17:31,925
[in English] Thank you.

370
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:34,094
Oh, slowly, my dear.

371
00:17:34,178 --> 00:17:36,180
- [Janine] Yes.
- [Audrey] There!

372
00:17:36,263 --> 00:17:37,765
[Audrey, in English] Thank you so much.

373
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:42,686
[melodramatic music playing]

374
00:17:52,237 --> 00:17:55,783
[light music playing]

375
00:17:57,701 --> 00:18:00,287
Why does it feel like we're not moving?

376
00:18:01,747 --> 00:18:03,290
Yes, I noticed that too.

377
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:09,630
Well, you're rowing that way.

378
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:10,756
I'm rowing this way.

379
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:13,425
- [Atoy] I thought--
- We really won't move. Hello?

380
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:14,927
Aren't we supposed to go there?

381
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:19,306
[chuckling]

382
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:21,934
- [Atoy] Oh my.
- Okay, I'll switch.

383
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:23,268
- [Audrey] I'll move, okay.
- [Atoy] Okay, okay.

384
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:25,187
[Audrey] Here, here. Okay, okay.

385
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,772
[Atoy grunts]

386
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:29,483
- Oh? What, here?
- Yes, okay.

387
00:18:29,566 --> 00:18:30,567
- All right, go.
- Oh, let's go there.

388
00:18:30,651 --> 00:18:31,860
[in English] One, two, three, go.

389
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:34,530
Oh. [squeals]

390
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:35,447
[Atoy] Oh, sorry.

391
00:18:35,531 --> 00:18:36,824
- [Atoy] Sorry, I didn't--
- What was that?!

392
00:18:36,907 --> 00:18:38,242
Sorry, I didn't mean it.

393
00:18:38,325 --> 00:18:39,743
Ah, so that's how it is? Here, me too.

394
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:40,953
I didn't mean it either.

395
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:42,454
- [Atoy] Wait!
- [squeals, then chuckles]

396
00:18:42,538 --> 00:18:43,413
All right, let's go there.

397
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:46,250
- [Janine] Mommy!
- [in English] Sorry. Time-out, time-out.

398
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:48,669
Child, I'm sorry.

399
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:49,753
I'm really sorry.

400
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:51,421
- [Audrey] Okay.
- Face that way.

401
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,090
That's the dry part.

402
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:54,758
- [Atoy] Sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry.
- Sorry, sorry, child.

403
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:57,136
[Audrey squeals] My scarf!

404
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:58,887
[in English] Oh, no…

405
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:01,098
- Oh, no. It's expensive--[squeals]
- [Atoy] Oh my.

406
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:02,391
[Atoy] There, it's sinking!

407
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:03,851
- [Audrey] Oh my!
- Oh!

408
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:06,186
It's just a scarf.

409
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:07,479
[Audrey] Okay, I can do this.

410
00:19:07,563 --> 00:19:08,814
[suspicious music playing]

411
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:10,440
[in English] Come here, come here.

412
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:11,650
[in English] Got it. Almost got it!

413
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:13,026
- Mommy--
- [Audrey squeals]

414
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:15,362
[Janine] Mommy! Daddy, Mommy!

415
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:17,823
Let her. She can handle it!

416
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:20,701
[Atoy grunts]

417
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:22,035
Mommy.

418
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:23,704
[music fades]

419
00:19:23,787 --> 00:19:25,038
Mommy!

420
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:26,456
Daddy.

421
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,500
Daddy!

422
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:29,501
Audrey?

423
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:31,879
[ominous music playing]

424
00:19:31,962 --> 00:19:33,005
Audrey?

425
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,676
Mommy!

426
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:41,847
[foreboding music playing]

427
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:43,557
Audrey?

428
00:19:44,057 --> 00:19:45,309
Audrey!

429
00:19:45,392 --> 00:19:46,560
Mommy!

430
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:48,562
Mommy?

431
00:19:48,645 --> 00:19:50,063
Audrey!

432
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:54,443
[in English] I found it!
I found it! [pants]

433
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:56,445
I just swam because…

434
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:58,363
the water's cold.

435
00:19:58,447 --> 00:19:59,907
Son of a thread!

436
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:02,534
You scared us. We thought
something happened to you!

437
00:20:02,618 --> 00:20:04,703
I know how to swim.

438
00:20:04,786 --> 00:20:06,914
I lived on the island for a long time.

439
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,081
Did you forget?

440
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:09,958
Well, how would I know?
You've changed, right?

441
00:20:10,042 --> 00:20:11,710
For all I know, you forgot how to swim.

442
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:13,837
[in English] I may have a different name,

443
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:18,508
but I'm still the same girl
you met back then, Anthony.

444
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:21,428
[light music playing]

445
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:23,096
[in English] Race you back!
[chuckles softly]

446
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:34,566
[music fades]

447
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:41,323
You know, I still wonder
why Mom puts up with Dad.

448
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:44,534
She's used to him not being around.

449
00:20:45,118 --> 00:20:47,371
We're happier when he's not here.

450
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:49,248
Hmm…

451
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:53,293
Maybe your dad is your mom's true love.

452
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:55,087
That's why she puts up with everything,

453
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:57,673
because they've been
through a lot together.

454
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:00,092
Sis, I don't think so.

455
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:04,263
Well, aren't there couples like that?

456
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:05,180
They stay together,

457
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:07,599
even if they don't love
each other anymore,

458
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:10,519
because they're just used to it.
It's convenient.

459
00:21:11,228 --> 00:21:14,523
And maybe your mom
is afraid of growing old alone.

460
00:21:14,606 --> 00:21:16,608
[melanchoic music playing]

461
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:19,152
- [sighs]
- [Karla] Oh?

462
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:20,779
- [sighs]
- Mom!

463
00:21:20,862 --> 00:21:22,531
I thought you weren't going to work.

464
00:21:22,614 --> 00:21:24,199
I have something to finish.

465
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:27,119
And your father left.
Said he'd look for a job.

466
00:21:27,202 --> 00:21:28,745
Good thing!

467
00:21:31,039 --> 00:21:32,749
Um, Miss Cita, how about you?

468
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:36,169
Didn't you ever think of leaving,
look for another job?

469
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:39,256
Or maybe starting your own tailoring shop?

470
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:41,049
I'm happy here.

471
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:44,303
And Delfin asked me to guide Atoy.

472
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:47,514
He and his wife Julie
were my best friends.

473
00:21:47,597 --> 00:21:50,100
So, I'm just fulfilling my promise.

474
00:21:52,936 --> 00:21:54,146
Um, Miss Cita,

475
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:58,900
if you and Sir Delfin were single then,

476
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:01,028
do you think you could've been together?

477
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:03,322
[Karla] I wish that were the case, right?

478
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:05,073
Then Brother Atoy
and I would be your children.

479
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:07,034
[Ame] Mmm-mmm.

480
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:08,660
[Karla chuckles softly]

481
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:11,121
[mellow music playing]

482
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:16,960
- Oh, thank you.
- [Atoy grunts]

483
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:18,420
- Um…
- [groans]

484
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:20,964
- All right, all right.
- Oh.

485
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:22,007
Um, no.

486
00:22:22,090 --> 00:22:23,967
- It's okay. It's yours now.
- [Atoy] Here, here. Use it, use it.

487
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:26,136
[Janine] My daddy is so sweet!

488
00:22:26,219 --> 00:22:27,137
Ayiee!

489
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:28,597
- [Janine giggles]
- [Audrey] Janine…

490
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:30,223
Janine-- Come here.

491
00:22:30,307 --> 00:22:31,600
You need to change.

492
00:22:32,225 --> 00:22:35,937
Tatoy, there's a horseback
riding activity here.

493
00:22:36,438 --> 00:22:38,273
I want to ride a horse.

494
00:22:38,356 --> 00:22:39,191
Really?

495
00:22:39,941 --> 00:22:41,068
All right.

496
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:42,861
Go ahead first. I'll just change.

497
00:22:43,528 --> 00:22:44,362
[in English] Yes!

498
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:51,953
[tense music playing]

499
00:22:59,669 --> 00:23:00,796
Uh, little girl, hmm,

500
00:23:00,879 --> 00:23:02,714
we'll just take a 40-minute break, okay?

501
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:05,217
We'll also feed the horses first.

502
00:23:05,759 --> 00:23:06,843
Are you alone?

503
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:09,262
Uh, no.

504
00:23:09,971 --> 00:23:12,808
I'm waiting for my father.

505
00:23:12,891 --> 00:23:14,601
He's taking so long.

506
00:23:14,684 --> 00:23:17,270
Mmm. Better go to him first.

507
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:18,563
Just come back later.

508
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:21,608
Ah, yes.

509
00:23:23,401 --> 00:23:26,404
[pensive music playing]

510
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:31,743
[Audrey] Atoy, Atoy!

511
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:33,078
Don't leave yet. Stay here first.

512
00:23:33,161 --> 00:23:37,207
Um, Janine requested that
we surprise her with a birthday cake.

513
00:23:38,208 --> 00:23:40,168
She requested a surprise?

514
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:41,962
How will that be a surprise?

515
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:44,131
Um, just let it be.

516
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:46,133
She's been a good girl today.

517
00:23:46,716 --> 00:23:48,051
And…

518
00:23:48,844 --> 00:23:50,178
There she is. She's coming out!

519
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:51,304
- Oh.
- Give it to me.

520
00:23:51,388 --> 00:23:52,639
Light it now.

521
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:59,938
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you</i> ♪

522
00:24:00,021 --> 00:24:04,609
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you</i> ♪

523
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:10,448
♪ <i>Happy birthday, happy birthday</i> ♪

524
00:24:10,949 --> 00:24:15,537
♪ <i>Happy birthday to you</i> ♪

525
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:17,122
Thank you, Mommy and Daddy.

526
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:20,333
[in English] Don't forget to make a wish
before you blow your candle, dear.

527
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:23,420
I wish my parents would get back together,

528
00:24:23,503 --> 00:24:26,423
so our family of three will be complete!

529
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:30,594
- Wow!
- [staff] Yay!

530
00:24:30,677 --> 00:24:32,387
Oh, were you surprised?

531
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:33,597
[chuckles softly]

532
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:35,432
- Oh, let's take a picture!
- [indistinct]

533
00:24:35,515 --> 00:24:36,600
- [in English] Let's go, let's go.
- [indistinct]

534
00:24:36,683 --> 00:24:37,809
[staff] We'll post it
on our social media page.

535
00:24:37,893 --> 00:24:38,727
- [Audrey] Okay.
- [Atoy] Yes.

536
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:40,478
Smile, child! Happy birthday!

537
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:41,479
[in English] Thank you.

538
00:24:41,563 --> 00:24:43,815
[in English] One, two, three!
Say, "Happy family!"

539
00:24:43,899 --> 00:24:46,693
- [all, in English] Happy family!
- [camera shutter snaps]

540
00:24:47,694 --> 00:24:49,029
[staff, in English] One more, one more.

541
00:24:50,071 --> 00:24:52,532
Mommy, Daddy, kiss each other.

542
00:24:53,116 --> 00:24:54,034
- [Atoy] Huh?
- Oh?

543
00:24:54,117 --> 00:24:56,494
- [Janine] Please kiss, please.
- Yiee, they'll get back together!

544
00:24:56,578 --> 00:24:57,579
[teasing]

545
00:24:57,662 --> 00:24:59,915
- [titters]
- Get back together?

546
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:01,249
- [Janine] Please.
- [mutters]

547
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:04,169
- Huh?
- Kiss, kiss each other. Please, kiss.

548
00:25:04,252 --> 00:25:06,129
- Kiss.
- Hey, kiss. Your child is requesting.

549
00:25:06,213 --> 00:25:07,797
- [staff] I'll take another picture.
- On the cheeks only, okay?

550
00:25:08,673 --> 00:25:10,342
Of course. Why,
did you want it on the lips?

551
00:25:11,301 --> 00:25:12,594
Stop it, Atoy.

552
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:14,554
- All right.
- Okay, kiss.

553
00:25:15,388 --> 00:25:16,765
- [staff, in English] One, two, three.
- [camera shutter snaps]

554
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:19,267
[staff, in English] Hold it, hold it.

555
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:20,352
[camera shutter snaps]

556
00:25:20,435 --> 00:25:22,229
Oh, come on. You too.

557
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,772
Oh, one more. One more.

558
00:25:23,855 --> 00:25:24,731
One, two--

559
00:25:26,149 --> 00:25:27,484
Oh, that's enough.

560
00:25:32,572 --> 00:25:36,284
[tense music playing]

561
00:25:42,290 --> 00:25:43,124
UP NEXT

562
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:44,709
She's the one who threw it, not me!

563
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:46,461
You lying child!

564
00:25:46,544 --> 00:25:47,420
[cracks]

565
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:49,547
I didn't like what you did to my child.

566
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:50,465
[man] You're the mother of that child?

567
00:25:50,548 --> 00:25:51,967
No wonder she's unruly.

568
00:25:52,550 --> 00:25:53,927
You're arrogant.

569
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:55,053
You think you're somebody.

570
00:25:56,346 --> 00:25:57,639
[Ibyang] <i>Let's not follow them.</i>

571
00:25:57,722 --> 00:25:59,474
That person is dangerous.

572
00:25:59,557 --> 00:26:00,517
[Ibyang] <i>He has a gun.</i>

573
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,768
Are you his wife?

574
00:26:03,144 --> 00:26:05,230
[dramatic stinging]

575
00:26:05,814 --> 00:26:07,482
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

576
00:26:07,565 --> 00:26:09,901
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

577
00:26:09,985 --> 00:26:13,905
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

578
00:26:13,989 --> 00:26:16,449
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
